  "inclusion_rules": [
    "Canonical time index is the hour-ending UTC timestamp ('UTC Time at End of Hour'); rows are de-duplicated on (BA, UTC) only if exact duplicates (none found).",
    "Reported 'Demand (MW)' is the analysis variable. Blank values are kept as missing (never zero-filled).",
    "Non-positive reported demand (0 MW) is physically invalid for an interconnection-scale BA aggregate and is treated as naturally invalid (missing).",
    "Naturally invalid hours are not scored, not labeled, and never used as injection sites.",
    "Extreme positive demand values (e.g., heat-wave peaks) are retained; no outlier trimming of the background.",
    "EIA 'Demand Forecast', 'Net Generation', and imputed/adjusted columns are not detector inputs (leakage/scope control); they are used only for the data-quality audit.",
